      "premise_index": 0,
      "exact_statement": "BEGZ, arXiv:0812.3674v2, §1.2, Definitions 1.1–1.2 and Propositions 1.4/1.6: For local psh u₁,…,uₚ on a complex n-manifold, 1≤p≤n, the nonpluripolar product is determined by 1_{∩{uⱼ>−N}}⋀ⱼddᶜmax(uⱼ,−N), provided these currents have uniformly bounded local masses. When defined, it is positive, depends only on the currents, is plurifine-local and charges no pluripolar set. If the potentials are locally bounded outside a closed locally complete pluripolar Z, existence is equivalent to local finiteness near Z of the complement’s Bedford–Taylor product; the result is its trivial extension. Products of closed positive (1,1)-currents on compact Kähler manifolds always exist.",
